.SH NAME
passgen \- command‑line password generator with clipboard integration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B passgen
.RI [ options ] " [length]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBpassgen\fR generates random passwords, passphrases, and tokens using a variety of secure algorithms and copies the result to the system clipboard (supporting Wayland, X11, and macOS). By default it creates a password of 16 characters using cryptographically secure random sources. The length can be overridden by providing a numeric argument or by using options.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.B \-n, \-\-no\-clip
Do not copy to clipboard (print to standard output only).
.TP
.B \-c, \-\-count \fIN\fR
Generate \fIN\fR passwords or passphrases.
.TP
.B \-l, \-\-length \fIN\fR
Set the password length to \fIN\fR characters (default: 16).
.TP
.B \-w, \-\-words [\fIN\fR]
Generate a multi-word Diceware-style passphrase composed of \fIN\fR random words (default: 4).
.TP
.B \-p, \-\-pin [\fIN\fR]
Generate a numeric PIN of \fIN\fR digits (default: 16).
.TP
.B \-\-osc52
Emit an ANSI OSC 52 terminal copy escape sequence (allows clipboard synchronization over SSH).
.TP
.B \-\-clear \fIseconds\fR
Automatically clear the clipboard after the specified number of seconds.
.TP
.B \-l, \-\-long
Generate a set of long hash‑style passwords.
.TP
.B \-a, \-\-all, \-v
Generate all password types: obedient, disobedient and long passwords.
.TP
.B \-o, \-\-obedient
Generate an “obedient” password that respects the requested length.
.TP
.B \-u, \-\-unsafe [\fIlength\fR]
Generate an unfiltered printable ASCII password stream.
.TP
.B \-t, \-\-test
Run a self‑test exercising each generator routine.
.SH EXAMPLES
Generate a 16‑character password and copy it to the clipboard:
.PP
.nf
$ passgen
.fi
.PP
Generate a 24-character password without copying to clipboard:
.PP
.nf
$ passgen 24 \-n
.fi
.PP
Generate a 5-word Diceware passphrase:
.PP
.nf
$ passgen \-w 5
.fi
.PP
Generate 5 passwords at once:
.PP
.nf
$ passgen \-c 5 \-n
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR apg (1),
.BR pwgen (1),
.BR xclip (1),
.BR wl-copy (1),
.BR gpg (1),
